WEBVTT

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.230
<b>Yuu</b>

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.230
<b>Incoming Call</b>

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.230
<b>Answer</b>

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.230
<b>Reject</b>

00:00:06.730 --> 00:00:08.230
Oh, it's Yuu.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.820
Hello?

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.080
Yeah, what's up?

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.740
I thought you were going to your 
older cousin's place today.

00:00:14.740 --> 00:00:17.250
<i>Help me, Jun!</i>

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.620
Huh? What's wrong?

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:20.750
You're scaring me.

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.200
Aren't you in Osaka to help her move?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:26.250
<i>Actually...</i>

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.790
I'm in Nagoya right now, and...

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:33.010
I'm lost!

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.410
<i>What?</i>

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.490
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:00:55.490 --> 00:00:56.030
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:00:56.030 --> 00:00:56.950
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.480
<b>Nagoya</b>

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.480
Help me!

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:16.200
Yuu, I don't understand 
what you're talking about.

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.240
What's going on? What happened?

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:21.720
<i>Nagoya? I thought you went to Osaka?</i>

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.250
Yeah.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:28.340
I was on the bullet train going home with my 
brother and cousin just a little while ago.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.090
<i>We will soon arrive at Nagoya.</i>

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.580
<i>After departing Nagoya, 
the next stop is Shin-Yokohama.</i>

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:45.960
I saw someone from the window who 
kind of looked like Koizumi-san.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.770
<i>What is she doing here?!</i>

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:54.790
Yuu?

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:56.000
Goin' to the bathroom?

00:03:00.670 --> 00:03:03.970
I jumped off the train without thinking.

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.920
Both my cousin and my brother are asleep,

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:07.830
and they won't answer their phones.

00:03:08.660 --> 00:03:13.790
<b>Disgust.</b>

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.680
Yuu, you're such a moron!

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.130
I bet that wasn't even her.

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:16.540
Koizumi-san was there.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.640
I would never mistake anyone for her.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.550
<i>Don't suddenly sound all serious.</i>

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.560
Just come back to Tokyo.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.050
<i>I don't have any money.</i>

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.180
All I had in my pocket was a 500-yen coin.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:27.900
Seriously?

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.680
You got off the train empty-handed?!

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.310
<i>Jeez...</i>

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:36.620
All right, I'll try calling Koizumi-san.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.940
I doubt she's actually in Nagoya, but still...

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:42.200
<i>And I'll try texting her.</i>

00:03:42.500 --> 00:03:45.450
I can give her your address, right, Yuu?

00:03:45.450 --> 00:03:49.450
<i>Huh? Why do they have her number, and I don't?</i>

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:48.620
<b>Huh? Why do they have her number, and I don't?</b>

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:49.450
<i>I'm gonna hang up for now, okay?</i>

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.150
Oh... Right. Thanks.

00:03:55.660 --> 00:03:56.460
<i>Huh?</i>

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:59.680
<i>I'm the only one who doesn't know it?!</i>

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:10.570
Koizumi-san? Where are you?

00:04:14.510 --> 00:04:16.310
Koizumi-san?

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:18.510
Golden...

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:25.980
Koizumi-san, where are you?

00:04:27.940 --> 00:04:29.900
That kishimen looks good.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:34.470
Koizumi-san would definitely 
be in a ramen shop, though.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:37.070
Silver...

00:04:40.710 --> 00:04:45.720
<b>Mitsuki Station Hotel</b>

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:44.850
Hey, Koizumi-san!

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.430
Maybe she's over here.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:53.390
Please come out now!

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.020
I'm so hungry.

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.520
But I only have 500 yen.

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:11.950
Is this...

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:15.820
a ramen shop?

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:19.380
<b>Taiwanese Mazesoba</b>

00:05:20.470 --> 00:05:21.730
Welcome.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:28.430
<i>It looked like I could actually get something
with my one coin here, so I came in.</i>

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:32.320
<i>Kind of looks like a fast-food place.</i>

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:35.740
<i>It is a ramen place, though, right?</i>

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:42.150
<i>Even at a time like this, 
I end up choosing ramen.</i>

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:45.340
<i>I've changed a lot, and we
all know who's responsible.</i>

00:05:45.340 --> 00:05:48.280
Number two, your order is ready!

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:49.700
That's me!

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.690
One ramen with egg?

00:05:51.690 --> 00:05:53.000
That's right.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:54.700
Enjoy your meal.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:58.880
I'm so hungry!

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.210
Time to eat.

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.640
I'll start with the soup.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:04.710
It was cold outside.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:06.650
<i>What is this?</i>

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.220
<i>This... isn't a soup spoon.</i>

00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:12.130
<i>What the heck is this?</i>

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.180
Here you go!

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.390
<i>They're eating their noodles with this!</i>

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:21.020
<i>But that guy is using chopsticks.</i>

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.480
<i>So we've got this weird spork, or chopsticks.</i>

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:26.500
Which one should I use?

00:06:28.060 --> 00:06:29.730
Which one is the right one?

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:37.250
Why don't you eat with 
whichever one you like best?

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.180
Ko—

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.510
Incidentally, I eat half 
of it with chopsticks,

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:48.130
and when it's time to pierce the egg,
I switch to the ramen fork.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:52.340
I feel like the updated design 
has made them even easier to use,

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:54.680
<b>Old</b>

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:57.390
since you can now eat the noodles and 
the soup with egg at the same time.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.390
<b>New</b>

00:06:57.640 --> 00:07:04.020
<b>Spellbound</b>

00:06:57.700 --> 00:07:00.470
Your beauty is recognized worldwide.

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:00.060
<b>Artifact from the
New York Museum of Modern Art</b>

00:07:01.330 --> 00:07:04.040
Tremble      Tremble

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:05.820
K-K-Koizumi-san!

00:07:05.820 --> 00:07:07.480
You came to rescue me!

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.140
You <i>were</i> in Nagoya!

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:10.110
Huh?

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.360
What do you mean?

00:07:11.640 --> 00:07:17.030
Oh, come on. Jun and Misa contacted you, 
and you came to pick me up, right?

00:07:17.030 --> 00:07:18.290
Contacted?

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.900
Oh, yeah. Looks like I have 
a missed call and a text.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:23.040
What? This was really a coincidence?

00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:31.180
Then again, meeting randomly on a trip 
makes it seem even more like destiny!

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.050
I don't know if I'd call it destiny.

00:07:33.700 --> 00:07:38.420
Coming to Nagoya and <i>not</i> getting ramen 
and soft serve here simply isn't an option.

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:40.820
Anyway, it's going to get cold.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:41.970
You're right.

00:07:41.970 --> 00:07:43.120
Time to eat.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.940
And I'm going to use this!

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:58.390
<i>It's like...</i>

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:13.160
<i>This makes me feel so relieved.</i>

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.250
I feel so at ease.

00:08:21.590 --> 00:08:26.140
It looks like we have another hour 
before the bullet train departs.

00:08:26.140 --> 00:08:28.160
There's time for one more 
bowl to wrap up the day.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.070
Huh? What are you saying?

00:08:30.500 --> 00:08:31.480
Wait!

00:08:31.480 --> 00:08:33.810
You don't have to come with me.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:36.660
No, I can't get home without you!

00:08:36.660 --> 00:08:39.700
<b>Heya!
I don't particularly need anything from you,
but it seems like Yuu got off the bullet train
empty-handed in Nagoya!
lol!!
Are you in Nagoya right now~?
If you are, can you please get in touch with her?
I'll attach her address.</b>

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:39.700
You read Misa's text, right?

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.140
How come you're in Nagoya, anyway?

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:45.370
I thought you went back to Tokyo last night.

00:08:47.110 --> 00:08:48.180
Well...

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.510
Yesterday, on the bullet train back to Tokyo,

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.460
the magazine I was reading had an 
article about Taiwanese mazesoba.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:56.090
Oh, Nagoya...

00:08:56.600 --> 00:09:00.540
Before I knew it, I was at the store in Nagoya
that's the birthplace of Taiwanese ramen.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:04.710
<b>Phew</b>

00:09:00.540 --> 00:09:02.000
A perfect blend of spicy and tasty.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.140
The ground meat and the leek 
are what make it special.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.580
Wow, I didn't know you could 
get Taiwanese ramen in Nagoya.

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:10.480
You can't.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:14.240
It's a local specialty of Nagoya 
that a Taiwanese chef created.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.370
The dish doesn't exist in Taiwan itself.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.240
<b>Taiwan</b>

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:23.290
By the way, I ordered my ramen in 
the not-so-spicy "American style."

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.320
I'm not super into spicy food.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:28.560
Wait, but how do you make a 
Taiwanese dish American style?

00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:32.130
Just like with Americano coffee,
the "American" means it's not so strong.

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:41.140
<b>Ramen</b>

00:09:32.720 --> 00:09:36.480
Right now, Taiwanese ramen is 
a major attraction in Nagoya.

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:41.140
This is a different restaurant, 
but naturally, this chain has it as well.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.710
Welcome!

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:51.380
I get the feeling this ramen is 
trying to evoke "betocon ramen."

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:52.400
Beto...?

00:09:52.400 --> 00:10:03.540
<b>Betocon Ramen</b>

00:09:52.610 --> 00:09:57.270
It's South Vietnamese... no, it's a 
ramen that gives you a lot of energy

00:09:57.270 --> 00:09:58.630
and puts you in your best condition.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:01.640
It does look like it would 
give you a lot of stamina.

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:03.540
And it looks pretty spicy.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:07.730
It's not as intensely spicy as 
Hokkyoku or Karakarauo,

00:10:07.730 --> 00:10:10.000
so if you can handle those, 
you'd be fine with this.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.430
I suppose it depends on your personal limits.

00:10:12.430 --> 00:10:14.500
Right. I have no idea what you mean.

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:18.480
I'm going to order mine 
without any crushed garlic.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.350
Really, I'd like to go triple, but...

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:23.260
...you're about to get on the bullet train.

00:10:24.240 --> 00:10:25.920
Two servings of Taiwan ramen.

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:27.770
Thank you for waiting!

00:10:28.140 --> 00:10:30.540
They gave us a spoon with holes.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:32.870
So you can fish out the ground meat easier.

00:10:32.870 --> 00:10:34.520
I see. Well, then...

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:36.580
Time to eat.

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.830
The leek smells so good.

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:48.960
It's so hot!

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.540
But that's what's good about it.

00:11:09.810 --> 00:11:11.660
Thank you for the food.

00:11:13.510 --> 00:11:16.150
It's almost time to get on the train.

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:20.790
I'll pay you back for the ramen 
and the bullet train ticket.

00:11:20.790 --> 00:11:23.080
I'm really sorry.

00:11:23.080 --> 00:11:26.540
Jumping off a train without concern for 
where you end up is very like you.

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.790
What were you even thinking?

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:32.560
I'm just...

00:11:37.220 --> 00:11:43.890
I'm just obsessed with Koizumi-san,
the girl who's obsessed with ramen!

00:11:45.600 --> 00:11:50.460
I-I've never felt anything like that before.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:58.080
Which is why I was hoping we could 
maybe become better friends.

00:12:00.280 --> 00:12:01.640
The train is about to leave.

00:12:02.380 --> 00:12:04.160
Let's sit next to each other!

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.780
We don't have reserved seats!

00:12:10.950 --> 00:12:13.540
<b>1 new message from
koizumi@...

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:17.580
<i>This address is...</i>

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:20.710
<i>I can give her your address, right, Yuu?</i>

00:12:21.140 --> 00:12:22.380
<i>This can't be.</i>

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:23.620
<i>This can't be!</i>

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:25.970
<b>From:
Subject:

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:25.970
<i>No.</i>

00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:29.220
<i>My first text from Koizumi-san!</i>

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:32.350
<b>Ahhhhhh</b>

00:12:30.340 --> 00:12:37.020
<i>Finally... Finally, we're texting each other!</i>

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:44.860
<b>Bro
Bro
Bro
Bro
Bro
Bro
Bro</b>

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.500
<i>My brother's called me a million times!</i>

00:12:43.500 --> 00:12:45.070
<i>I completely forgot about him!</i>

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.910
What were you doing?

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:50.680
I was eating ramen.

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:53.620
Do you know how worried I was?!

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.820
I'm really sorry.

00:12:56.360 --> 00:12:58.780
I didn't even notice.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:03.170
<b>Stare</b>

00:13:00.410 --> 00:13:03.630
<i>I haven't gotten a text
from Koizumi-san since.</i>

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:05.890
<i>I wonder who she's writing to...</i>

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:09.120
Oh, they sent me a coupon 
for a hard-boiled egg add-on.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:09.970
<b>Only uses LINE and texts
for ramen shops</b>

00:13:12.470 --> 00:13:14.980
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:20.480
<b>Reunion</b>

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:18.890
<i>One day in autumn...</i>

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.570
<i>Koizumi-san caught a cold.</i>

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.600
K-Koizumi-san, are you okay?

00:13:47.630 --> 00:13:48.800
I'm fine.

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.340
But you look miserable.

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:51.990
Don't you have a fever?

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:53.680
Are you really okay?

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:56.140
I know! I could take care of you!

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:57.840
I'll visit you at your house.

00:13:57.840 --> 00:13:58.840
There's no need.

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:01.770
Please don't come.

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.820
She looked pretty sick.

00:14:08.240 --> 00:14:09.540
It's not like her at all.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:12.400
I thought she didn't even catch colds.

00:14:12.400 --> 00:14:14.650
It did suddenly get cold yesterday.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:17.200
She was probably standing 
in some line forever.

00:14:21.260 --> 00:14:22.850
Koizumi-san...

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:29.300
In that sense, this is a literary classic

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:32.430
that has been read and loved 
by many, many people

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.930
over the course of many generations.

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:38.860
We're going to read it again with that in mind.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:38.860
<i>Koizumi-san didn't come to school today.</i>

00:14:48.560 --> 00:14:49.860
<i>Or the next day...</i>

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:56.810
<i>Or the day after that.</i>

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:15.320
Ma'am, you have to tell me 
Koizumi-san's address!

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:17.390
Please calm down, Ohsawa-san.

00:15:17.390 --> 00:15:19.600
She might be really sick!

00:15:19.600 --> 00:15:21.650
Koizumi-san is fine.

00:15:21.900 --> 00:15:23.520
We got a call from her this morning.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.650
But I really think it'd be 
better if I were there!

00:15:25.650 --> 00:15:28.150
<b>Yuu: Are you okay?
Yuu: I'm worried about you
Yuu: I'll come visit you!
Yuu: I'll make ramen for you</b>

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:30.290
Pull yourself together, Yuu.

00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:34.070
She won't return my texts.

00:15:34.070 --> 00:15:36.710
She has a cold. She's probably sleeping.

00:15:36.710 --> 00:15:39.410
We need to let her get some rest, right?

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:41.080
What is she eating, though?

00:15:41.080 --> 00:15:42.500
Is there anyone to look after her?

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:44.290
What if she collapses all alone?

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:47.100
The school got a call. She's fine.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:48.160
Jun's right.

00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.010
We're talking about Koizumi.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:53.640
Why, Koizumi-san?!

00:15:53.640 --> 00:15:57.080
You can lean on me more, you know!

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:00.310
<i>But...</i>

00:16:02.810 --> 00:16:08.870
<i>Koizumi-san didn't return to 
school for quite some time.</i>

00:16:14.400 --> 00:16:16.720
<i>Then, today,</i>

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:22.830
<i>after a two-week absence, 
Koizumi-san came back to school.</i>

00:16:27.280 --> 00:16:28.800
See ya!

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:40.970
Huh?

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:43.560
Aren't you going home with Koizumi?

00:16:43.560 --> 00:16:45.430
You haven't seen her in so long.

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:46.560
Is everything okay?

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:49.180
Today... it's fine.

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:51.360
Huh? Why? What's wrong?!

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:54.980
No, I thought about inviting 
her to walk with me,

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.610
until a little while ago.

00:16:57.100 --> 00:16:58.020
But then...

00:16:58.510 --> 00:16:59.660
Koizumi-san!

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.940
I'm so glad you're well again!

00:17:01.940 --> 00:17:03.180
Let's walk home together!

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:04.220
No, thank you.

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:05.670
Oh, come on!

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.250
We could have ramen to 
celebrate your recovery!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.380
Ramen...

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:23.520
She said she's barely eaten anything from 
when she got sick until this morning.

00:17:24.340 --> 00:17:25.920
Which means that today...

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:33.570
will be the first time she's had
ramen in two whole weeks.

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.950
<b>Ogikubo Chinese Soba</b>

00:17:33.940 --> 00:17:36.950
<b>Harukiya</b>

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.600
Here you go.

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:55.010
Time to eat.

00:18:46.240 --> 00:18:47.850
Welcome.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:38.880
Thank you.

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.570
I'm so glad.

00:19:53.570 --> 00:19:55.960
Koizumi-san is completely back on her feet!

00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:57.840
She followed her after all...

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:04.340
<i>I'm going to keep chasing Koizumi-san, 
the girl who loves ramen noodles!</i>

00:20:05.140 --> 00:20:05.720
<b>Shiver</b>

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:08.470
Am I getting sick again?

00:20:10.800 --> 00:20:12.100
Koizumi-san!

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.020
Yuu, wait!

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:19.900
Hey, Koizumi-san.

00:20:21.590 --> 00:20:23.950
You're going to another 
restaurant after this, right?

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.070
Can I go with you?

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:28.740
You did end up following her.

00:20:29.110 --> 00:20:32.210
I kind of feel like having ramen now, too.

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:34.420
May I come?

00:20:36.120 --> 00:20:38.920
I don't really like to eat with other people,

00:20:39.570 --> 00:20:43.200
but if you really want to eat 
ramen, do as you please.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:44.570
Yes!

00:20:44.570 --> 00:20:47.600
We should eat out together every day, then!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:48.930
I decline.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:50.540
Aw...

00:20:51.720 --> 00:20:54.940
<b>We wish you a delicious ramen...</b>

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.940
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:36.000
<b>Thank you for the food!</b>
